  "interpretation": "New RTX 5090 sessions that arrive after idle start at back-to-back speed, and nothing else changes. With --gpu-keep-warm-ms 60000 the GPU stays out of its low-power idle states for 60 s after each request, so new sessions after 12-58 s of idle prefilled in 0.155-0.157 s instead of 0.253-0.304 s; the role corpus answered byte-identically to v0.8.1 with the argument on and off, requests arriving while a spin could still run changed time to first token by a median of -0.1 ms, and the hold draws about 71 W while it runs (about 2.3 W averaged over production's logged agent traffic). On the published image the profile gates, durability workload, publication barrier, probe set, shared-prefix capacity and stock OMP 18.3.0 session proof reproduce v0.8.1's results. The RTX 4090 package is unchanged and carries its v0.8.1 qualification. Automatic checkpoints stay best effort and universal warm reuse is not claimed; alphastorm/omp-ninfer#48 stays open until field confirmation.",
